c61bf27fb210e0dc849829d5c287936fcb3f73bc279e98af8a64ba4085b8309.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis.\n\n- Finally, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $6.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=6sin⁡(-x).$\n\nNotice that, because the sine function is odd, the $y$-axis reflection has the same effect as the $x$-axis reflection, i.e.,\n\n$$\n6sin⁡(-x)=-6sin⁡x.\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=-6sin⁡x.$ However, $y=-6sin⁡x$ is not among the given options." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118443/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "85090bdf-4f1b-5f79-a751-48521ad98895"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118443"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-65833"] :question/worked-solution "The given curve is the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\nNotice that, because the cosine function is even, it is symmetric about the $y$-axis, i.e.,\n\n$$\ncos⁡(-x)=cos⁡x\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=cos⁡(-x).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-66202/selection/34a2bb4ca829f84541262951f16b64281d9165254937ea530c836afecf06b06a" :answer/id #uuid "6772008a-abb7-5543-a79d-8622da3c2a58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=sin⁡(-x)-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66202/selection/cb53ee02fb36399f949e5b4437880bcb08c587b892029b62c923687dd8c4439f" :answer/id #uuid "5fc64020-78b6-5774-b9e0-9cbfad1dbcd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=sin⁡(x)+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66202/selection/ed2b637b0ac22c3439c42329a9a725312ce23d729e836d88a1472cbbf4194783" :answer/id #uuid "d6060610-827b-5a3d-9623-441d88362ddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-2sin⁡(x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/i